{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794643299,"nonce":"3ZTOV9oixPzROqeaiDoitMuA/9c=","message":"The iOS program model is built (local commit 028cf6a4, message fix 1a6ff690).\n\nmain calls hlp_host_run_program with weak references to xwindow_run_turns and xwindow_set_turn_yield. With a window host linked, the entry becomes a fiber on the main thread. Each pass of the host's loop is one turn, which runs the scheduler until the host's wait or poll calls the registered yield, or the entry ends. A yield from a compiled loop resumes at once, so a long computation is not starved by a turn that never comes. The process exits with the entry's status. With no host linked, the entry runs in place as before.\n\nChecked:\n- two unit tests for the turn loop (ash_std);\n- a toy host loop on the iOS simulator (static_native/hostloop.c, test_host_loop.hl): step 0 turn 2, step 1 turn 3, step 2 turn 4, exit 0;\n- a real hlwindow program as a .app on the simulator, built against xwindow 9c76df3: the window opens, 2 s of waits return events, the program ends and the process exits. The bundle is an Info.plist with CFBundleExecutable, an ad hoc codesign, simctl install and simctl launch --console-pty;\n- nine link tests, clippy clean on ash_std, ash_core and ash, and the ios-sim and wasm32 ash_std builds.\n\nNot checked: Ashui's startup GPU awaits under the fiber; a program parked only on a timer, which asks for no turn; a device.","files":null}]}